## panel VARs {background-color="#FFD800"}

### featured models {style="color:#0056B9;"}

- country-specific VARs with global prior
- country-specific VARs with global prior by [Jarociński (2010, JAE)](https://doi.org/10.1002/jae.1082)
- country-grouping VARs with global prior
- country-specific VARs with global prior grouping
- country-specific VARs

### featured model specifications {style="color:#1A003F;"}

- VAR lag order modification
- exogenous variables
- constrained forecasting of rates
- prior hyper-parameters adjustment
- global prior mean set to pooled estimator by [Zellner, Hong (1989, JOE)](https://doi.org/10.1016/0304-4076(89)90036-5)











## panel VARs {background-color="#FFD800"}

### model with country grouping {style="color:#0056B9;"}

Let each country belong to a group $c\in g = \{1,\dots,G\}$.

Country-specific parameters become group-specific parameters.

\begin{align}
&\\
		\mathbf{y}_{c.t} &= \mathbf{A}_{g.1} \mathbf{y}_{c.t-1} + \mathbf{A}_{d.g}\mathbf{x}_{c.t} + \boldsymbol\epsilon_{c.t}\\[1ex]
		\boldsymbol\epsilon_{c.t}\mid \mathbf{y}_{c.t-1} & \sim N_4\left(\mathbf{0}_4, \boldsymbol\Sigma_g\right)\\[1ex]
		E_\pi\left[\mathbf{A}_{g}\right] &= \mathbf{A}\\[1ex]
		E_\pi\left[\boldsymbol\Sigma_c\right] &= \boldsymbol\Sigma\\
\end{align}		
		

## panel VARs {background-color="#FFD800"}

### model with country grouping {style="color:#0056B9;"}

```{r}
#| label: specg
#| cache: true
#| warning: false
#| eval: false

c_select = c("UKR","FRA","ESP","SWE","NOR",
             "DEU","FIN","POL","ITA","GBR")

specg = bvarGroupPANEL$new(
  ilo_dynamic_panel[c_select],
  exogenous = ilo_exogenous_variables[c_select],
  group_allocation = c(1,2,2,1,2,2,1,1,2,2)
)


burng = estimate(specg, S = 5000, show_progress = FALSE)
postg = estimate(burng, S = 5000)
```







## panel VARs {background-color="#FFD800"}

### model with global prior grouping {style="color:#0056B9;"}

Let each country belong to a group $c\in g = \{1,\dots,G\}$.

Country-specific parameters have group-specific prior mean.

\begin{align}
&\\
		\mathbf{y}_{c.t} &= \mathbf{A}_{c.1} \mathbf{y}_{c.t-1} + \mathbf{A}_{d.c}\mathbf{x}_{c.t} + \boldsymbol\epsilon_{c.t}\\[1ex]
		\boldsymbol\epsilon_{c.t}\mid \mathbf{y}_{c.t-1} & \sim N_4\left(\mathbf{0}_4, \boldsymbol\Sigma_c\right)\\[1ex]
		E_\pi\left[\mathbf{A}_{c}\right] &= \mathbf{A}_g\\[1ex]
		E_\pi\left[\boldsymbol\Sigma_c\right] &= \boldsymbol\Sigma_g\\
\end{align}		
		

## panel VARs {background-color="#FFD800"}

### model with global prior grouping {style="color:#0056B9;"}

```{r}
#| label: specgp
#| cache: true
#| warning: false
#| eval: false

c_select = c("UKR","FRA","ESP","SWE","NOR",
             "DEU","FIN","POL","ITA","GBR")

specp = bvarGroupPriorPANEL$new(
  ilo_dynamic_panel[c_select],
  exogenous = ilo_exogenous_variables[c_select],
  group_allocation = c(1,2,2,1,2,2,1,1,2,2)
)


burnp = estimate(specp, S = 5000, show_progress = FALSE)
postp = estimate(burnp, S = 5000)
```








