```




## forecasting {background-color="#FFD800"}

## forecasting {background-color="#FFD800"}

### forecasting features {style="color:#0056B9;"}

- original non-stationary variables
- point and density forecasting
- forecasting for models with exogenous variables
- restricted forecasting of rates
- marginal forecasts of labour market indicators
- expanding-window recursive forecasting
- forecast performance evaluation 
- forecast error variance decomposition





## forecasting {background-color="#FFD800"}

### one-period-ahead conditional predictive density {style="color:#0056B9;"}

\begin{align}
&\\
		{\color{lig}p\left(\mathbf{y}_{c.t+1}\mid \mathbf{y}_{c.t},\mathbf{A}_{c},\boldsymbol\Sigma_c\right)} & = N_4\left(\mathbf{A}_{c.1} \mathbf{y}_{c.t} + \mathbf{A}_{d.c}\mathbf{x}_{c.t+1}, \boldsymbol\Sigma_c\right)\\[5ex]
\end{align}
		
- implied by the model
- equivalent to the frequentist predictive density

### joint predictive density {style="color:#0056B9;"}

\begin{align}
		p\left(\mathbf{y}_{c.t+h},\dots,\mathbf{y}_{c.t+1}\mid \mathbf{Y}_{c.t}\right)
		&= \int p\left(\mathbf{y}_{c.t+h},\dots,\mathbf{y}_{c.t+1},\mathbf{A}_{c},\boldsymbol\Sigma_c\mid \mathbf{Y}_{c.t}\right)d\left(\mathbf{A}_{c},\boldsymbol\Sigma_c\right)
\end{align}

- accounts for parameter uncertainty
- used to generate forecast summaries




## forecasting {background-color="#FFD800"}

```{r}
#| label: for
#| cache: true
#| warning: false

fore = forecast(
  post,
  horizon = 3,
  exogenous_forecast = ilo_exogenous_forecasts,
) 
plot(fore, "UKR", main = "Forecasts for Ukraine")
```



## forecasting {background-color="#FFD800"}

- $UR$ forecasts for Poland are negative

```{r}
#| label: forpol
#| cache: true
#| warning: false
 
plot(fore, "POL", main = "Forecasts for Poland")
```



## constrained forecasting {background-color="#FFD800"}

- argument `type` set to `"rate"` constraints the forecasts to $[0,100]$

```{r}
#| label: forpolc
#| cache: true
#| warning: false
#| output-location: slide

ilo_dynamic_panel[c_select] |> 
  specify_bvarPANEL$new(
    exogenous = ilo_exogenous_variables[c_select],
    type = c("real","rate","rate","rate")
  ) |> 
  estimate(S = 5000, show_progress = FALSE) |> 
  estimate(S = 5000, show_progress = FALSE) -> post

post |>
  forecast(
    horizon = 3,
    exogenous_forecast = ilo_exogenous_forecasts,
  ) |> 
  plot(which_c = "POL", main = "Constrained forecasts for Poland")
```




